    "raw": "Evolve tags into an embedded, provenance-tracked, PLURAL `Tag` field that\nunifies MANUAL tags (5da67f94, now on master) and AUTOMATIC semantic tags\n(ef4ad78d). ef4ad78d's semantic tagger and this tagadd work MERGE TOGETHER --\nthey land as one change, not as separate steps.\n\nWhat a tag is:\n- A short, free-form string: a high-level description of the todo.\n- Case-insensitive; stored downcased (normalize on write).\n- May contain spaces.\n- No taxonomy / controlled vocabulary.\n\nProvenance -- each tag carries a `manual` boolean:\n- manual=true  (user-added via tagadd): sticky. Never auto-deleted or\n  recalculated; survives edits to Summary/Body.\n- manual=false (automatic, semantic): DERIVED from Summary+Body. Cleared and\n  recalculated by `doctor` (see lifecycle).\n\nData model -- `Tag` is a PLURAL list; each element is an embedded object shaped\nlike Summary/Body, embedded INDIVIDUALLY (its own vectors per embedder), so\nevery tag is a first-class searchable unit rather than one blob:\n\n  \"Tag\": [\n    { \"raw\": \"todo tool\",  \"manual\": true,  \"apple\": [[...]] },\n    { \"raw\": \"embeddings\", \"manual\": false, \"apple\": [[...]] }\n  ]\n\n- get-json-path addresses a tag by index: `Tag.0.raw`, `Tag.1.raw`, ...\n- Embedding-machinery change: _EMBED_FIELDS today maps one field -> one\n  dict-with-raw (Summary, Body). `Tag` is a LIST of such dicts, so the embed\n  write path, clear-on-write, and search ranking must ITERATE Tag's elements\n  (embed / clear / rank each element's raw), not treat Tag as a single dict.\n\nEmbedding + tagging lifecycle (target; reuse the existing clear-on-write and\nlazy-backfill machinery -- \"you have this logic elsewhere\"):\n- Search auto-populates ALL missing embeddings (lazy backfill), each Tag\n  element included.\n- Clear-on-write: editing Summary.raw, Body.raw, or a tag's raw zeros that\n  unit's embedding vectors (existing _strip_field_vectors path, per element).\n- Cross-field invalidation: editing Summary OR Body also zeros the AUTOMATIC\n  tags (their elements + embeddings) and marks them for recompute, since auto\n  tags derive from Summary+Body. Manual tags untouched.\n- Doctor REDOES tagging: recompute automatic tag elements via the corpus\n  semantic tagger, persist them, repopulate their embeddings. Manual survive.\n\nCLI:\n- `tagadd` / `tagrm` subcommands add / remove a MANUAL tag element (downcased,\n  deduped). (Source note: requested as \"tagagg\"/\"tagrm\"; using tagadd/tagrm.)\n\nRelationship to prior work:\n- 5da67f94 (MERGED to master): manual flat `Tags` list (list of plain strings)\n  + set --tag/--untag + search --tag. This todo migrates that to the plural\n  embedded `Tag` element model.\n- ef4ad78d (done; branch UNMERGED, 13 commits): zero-shot semantic `tag`\n  command + corpus embedding + n-phrase mining. Merges together with this work.\n\nRelated consumer: the ls/search list display gains a tags output column.\n\nResolved / out of scope:\n- MIGRATION is a separate worked todo: 58e8f379 (migrate-to-latest -- versioned\n  schema migrator across db + file backends, schema-version meta, startup\n  check). The flat-`Tags`-strings -> plural-`Tag`-elements conversion is a\n  migration step there, NOT hand-rolled here.\n- SEARCH ranking is completely separate from this todo. Near-term behavior:\n  search all sources and rank purely by unit-normalized angle (cosine)\n  similarity; a few ranking constants may be introduced. Tag search is expected\n  to be the more useful signal in practice.\n\nWorking model (Opus orchestrator / Sonnet implementor): worked per\nskills/projectmanagement/PLAN.md -- the model-assignment doc for AC-gated\nWorkItems. Each WorkItem AC is a frozen test; a Sonnet subagent codes to green,\nand Opus (this model) authors the ACs, verifies the diff, and integrates."
  },
